# OKF bundle finding baseline — issue #697.
#
# Per-category finding counts frozen at their present value. The gate fails
# a category whose count is ABOVE its entry here, so the existing findings
# pass while NEW drift does not. A count that drops is tightened by the
# next --regen; RAISING an entry is a deliberate, reviewable diff that
# wants a reason in the commit message.
#
# These are not targets. The listed findings are what #631 (OKF adoption)
# exists to drive to zero; this file only stops them growing meanwhile.
#
# A category that reaches zero DISAPPEARS from this file rather than being
# listed as 0 -- the counts come from the findings actually emitted, so a
# category with none produces no line. Absence is the TIGHTER state, not a
# gap: an unlisted category has an implicit baseline of 0, so a single
# regression fails. okf-missing-type left this file that way (#991
# migrated the bundle to top-level `type:`); do not re-add it as a 0.
#
# Regenerate with: tests/validate-okf-bundle.sh --regen

memory-missing-why 80
